<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  The Gini ingredient brand element ("Powered by gini"). Shown when the client configuration lists
  the screen in ingredientBrandScreens.

  One image, not a composed layout. gc_powered_by_gini_badge carries the pill, the wordmark and the
  logo as path data, so there is no colour, dimension, text style or string resource behind this
  element for an integrator to override — the badge is switched on by the backend and deliberately
  has no integrator-facing switch, so its appearance must not move when an integrator restyles the
  SDK. It also reproduces the Figma component exactly rather than approximating its SF Pro letter
  shapes with Roboto.

  Sized by the drawable's own 90x24dp intrinsic size. The content description is the only text and
  is deliberately not translated: "Powered by Gini" is a brand lockup, and iOS pins the same string
  for the same reason (PP-2570 spec R11).
-->
<ImageView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:contentDescription="Powered by Gini"
    android:focusable="false"
    android:importantForAccessibility="yes"
    android:src="@drawable/gc_powered_by_gini_badge"
    tools:ignore="HardcodedText" />
